      {
        "name": "register",
        "doc": " Register (or overwrite) the caller's meta-address. Payable: attach storage\n (126 bytes = 0.00126 NEAR the first time; overwrites cost nothing); the excess is refunded.\n `spend_pub`: 33-byte compressed secp256k1 hex. `view_pub`: 32-byte X25519 hex.\n `mode`: \"contract\" (Mode B, default) or \"account\" (Mode A fallback).",
        "kind": "call",
        "modifiers": [
          "payable"
        ],
        "params": {
          "serialization_type": "json",
          "args": [
            {
              "name": "spend_pub",
              "type_schema": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            {
              "name": "view_pub",
              "type_schema": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            {
              "name": "mode",
              "type_schema": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "signer_id",
        "doc": " The MPC signer this contract forwards `sign` to.",
        "kind": "view",
        "result": {
          "serialization_type": "json",
          "type_schema": {
            "description": "NEAR Account Identifier.\n\nThis is a unique, syntactically valid, human-readable account identifier on the NEAR network.\n\n[See the crate-level docs for information about validation.](index.html#account-id-rules)\n\nAlso see [Error kind precedence](AccountId#error-kind-precedence).\n\n## Examples\n\n``` use near_account_id::AccountId;\n\nlet alice: AccountId = \"alice.near\".parse().unwrap();\n\nassert!(\"ƒelicia.near\".parse::<AccountId>().is_err()); // (ƒ is not f) ```",
            "type": "string"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "sweep",
        "doc": " Ask the MPC signer to sign `payloads[0]` for `derive(this_contract, path)`, authorised by an\n ECDSA signature `(sig, v)` over `sweep_digest(...)` by the stealth key `k_pub`.\n Anyone may submit (a relayer); the signature binds contract, path, domain, expiry and\n payload, so the submitter cannot change what gets signed. Attach >= 1 yoctoNEAR (excess\n refunded) and 300 Tgas. Returns the MPC `sign` result unchanged\n (`{\"scheme\":\"Secp256k1\",big_r,s,recovery_id}` or `{\"scheme\":\"Ed25519\",signature}`).",
        "kind": "call",
        "modifiers": [
          "payable"
        ],
        "params": {
          "serialization_type": "json",
          "args": [
            {
              "name": "path",
              "type_schema": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            {
              "name": "domain_id",
              "type_schema": {
                "type": "integer",
                "format": "uint8",
                "minimum": 0.0
              }
            },
            {
              "name": "payloads",
              "type_schema": {
                "type": "array",
                "items": {
                  "type": "string"
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "name": "expires_block",
              "type_schema": {
                "type": "integer",
                "format": "uint64",
                "minimum": 0.0
              }
            },
            {
              "name": "k_pub",
              "type_schema": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            {
              "name": "sig",
              "type_schema": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            {
              "name": "v",
              "type_schema": {
                "type": "integer",
                "format": "uint8",
                "minimum": 0.0
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "result": {
          "serialization_type": "json",
          "type_schema": {
            "$ref": "#/definitions/Promise"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "sweep_digest",
        "doc": " Helper for clients: the hex digest `sweep` expects `K` to sign (same inputs, no auth).",
        "kind": "view",
        "params": {
          "serialization_type": "json",
          "args": [
            {
              "name": "path",
              "type_schema": {
